{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-ecclesiastes-007",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 7,
  "title": "Ecclesiastes 7",
  "display_title": "Ecclesiastes 7",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "ecclesiastes",
  "book": "Ecclesiastes",
  "bookName": "Ecclesiastes",
  "bookOrder": 21,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 7,
  "sortOrder": 21007,
  "verseCount": 29,
  "aliases": [
    "Eccl",
    "Ecc",
    "Qoheleth"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "A good name is better than precious ointment; and the day of death than the day of one’s birth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "It is better to go to the house of mourning, than to go to the house of feasting: for that is the end of all men; and the living will lay it to his heart.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Sorrow is better than laughter: for by the sadness of the countenance the heart is made better.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "The heart of the wise is in the house of mourning; but the heart of fools is in the house of mirth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "It is better to hear the rebuke of the wise, than for a man to hear the song of fools.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "For as the crackling of thorns under a pot, so is the laughter of the fool: this also is vanity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Surely oppression maketh a wise man mad; and a gift destroyeth the heart.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Better is the end of a thing than the beginning thereof: and the patient in spirit is better than the proud in spirit.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Be not hasty in thy spirit to be angry: for anger resteth in the bosom of fools.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Say not thou, What is the cause that the former days were better than these? for thou dost not enquire wisely concerning this.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Wisdom is good with an inheritance: and by it there is profit to them that see the sun.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "For wisdom is a defence, and money is a defence: but the excellency of knowledge is, that wisdom giveth life to them that have it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Consider the work of God: for who can make that straight, which he hath made crooked?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "In the day of prosperity be joyful, but in the day of adversity consider: God also hath set the one over against the other, to the end that man should find nothing after him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "All things have I seen in the days of my vanity: there is a just man that perisheth in his righteousness, and there is a wicked man that prolongeth his life in his wickedness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Be not righteous over much; neither make thyself over wise: why shouldest thou destroy thyself ?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Be not over much wicked, neither be thou foolish: why shouldest thou die before thy time?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "It is good that thou shouldest take hold of this; yea, also from this withdraw not thine hand: for he that feareth God shall come forth of them all.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Wisdom strengtheneth the wise more than ten mighty men which are in the city.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "For there is not a just man upon earth, that doeth good, and sinneth not.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Also take no heed unto all words that are spoken; lest thou hear thy servant curse thee:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "For oftentimes also thine own heart knoweth that thou thyself likewise hast cursed others.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "All this have I proved by wisdom: I said, I will be wise; but it was far from me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "That which is far off, and exceeding deep, who can find it out?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "I applied mine heart to know, and to search, and to seek out wisdom, and the reason of things, and to know the wickedness of folly, even of foolishness and madness:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "And I find more bitter than death the woman, whose heart is snares and nets, and her hands as bands: whoso pleaseth God shall escape from her; but the sinner shall be taken by her.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Behold, this have I found, saith the preacher, counting one by one, to find out the account:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "Which yet my soul seeketh, but I find not: one man among a thousand have I found; but a woman among all those have I not found.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "Lo, this only have I found, that God hath made man upright; but they have sought out many inventions.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 7:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:7:29"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
